  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Let $P(1,-2,4)$ and $Q(-3,0,5).$ Find $|q-p|,$ where $p$ and $q$ are position vectors of $P$ and $Q$, respectively.\n\n$|q-p|=${{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OP} & =p=i-2j+4k, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{OQ} & =q=-3i+5k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates of $q-p,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q-p & =(-3i+5k)-(i-2j+4k) \\\\  & =-4i+2j+k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|q-p| & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
